build_windows_jni.sh always asks vcvarsall for the amd64 tools, so on an
ARM64 Windows the JNI DLL comes out as AMD64 and the ARM64 JVM refuses it
("Can't load AMD 64-bit .dll on a ARM 64-bit platform", run 35692632379).
Pick the native tools for the machine the build runs on.  CI only for now.

--- a/scripts/bootstrap/build_windows_jni.sh	2026-09-22 17:07:51
+++ b/scripts/bootstrap/build_windows_jni.sh	2026-09-22 17:07:51
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@
 pwd_drive="$(echo "$abs_pwd" | head -c2)"
 cat > "${VSTEMP}/windows_jni.bat" <<EOF
 @echo OFF
-@call "${VSVARS}" amd64
+@if "%PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE%"=="ARM64" (call "${VSVARS}" arm64) else (call "${VSVARS}" amd64)
 @$pwd_drive
 @cd "$abs_pwd"
 @set TMP=$(cygpath -a -w "${VSTEMP}")
